{"audio": "titus-01.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 120533, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2400, "text": "Titus, Chapter One."}, {"start_ms": 2400, "end_ms": 17333, "text": "Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God's elect, and the acknowledging of the truth which is after godliness; In hope of eternal life, which God, that cannot lie, promised before the world began;"}, {"start_ms": 17333, "end_ms": 33600, "text": "But hath in due times manifested his word through preaching, which is committed unto me according to the commandment of God our Saviour; To Titus, mine own son after the common faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ our Saviour."}, {"start_ms": 33600, "end_ms": 48933, "text": "For this cause left I thee in Crete, that thou shouldest set in order the things that are wanting, and ordain elders in every city, as I had appointed thee: If any be blameless, the husband of one wife, having faithful children not accused of riot or unruly."}, {"start_ms": 48933, "end_ms": 67467, "text": "For a bishop must be blameless, as the steward of God; not selfwilled, not soon angry, not given to wine, no striker, not given to filthy lucre; But a lover of hospitality, a lover of good men, sober, just, holy, temperate; Holding fast the faithful word as he hath been taught,"}, {"start_ms": 67467, "end_ms": 72533, "text": "that he may be able by sound doctrine both to exhort and to convince the gainsayers."}, {"start_ms": 72533, "end_ms": 85333, "text": "For there are many unruly and vain talkers and deceivers, specially they of the circumcision: Whose mouths must be stopped, who subvert whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for filthy lucre's sake."}, {"start_ms": 85333, "end_ms": 92133, "text": "One of themselves, even a prophet of their own, said, The Cretians are alway liars, evil beasts, slow bellies."}, {"start_ms": 92133, "end_ms": 93600, "text": "This witness is true."}, {"start_ms": 93600, "end_ms": 102800, "text": "Wherefore rebuke them sharply, that they may be sound in the faith; Not giving heed to Jewish fables, and commandments of men, that turn from the truth."}, {"start_ms": 102800, "end_ms": 112533, "text": "Unto the pure all things are pure: but unto them that are defiled and unbelieving is nothing pure; but even their mind and conscience is defiled."}, {"start_ms": 112533, "end_ms": 120533, "text": "They profess that they know God; but in works they deny him, being abominable, and disobedient, and unto every good work reprobate."}], "words": [{"t": "Titus,", "s": 565, "e": 968, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 1674, "e": 1997, "si": 0}, {"t": "One.", "s": 2158, "e": 2319, "si": 0}, {"t": "Paul,", "s": 3001, "e": 3341, "si": 1}, {"t": "a", "s": 3481, "e": 3501, "si": 1}, {"t": "servant", "s": 3581, "e": 3921, "si": 1}, {"t": "of", "s": 3941, "e": 4021, "si": 1}, {"t": "God,", "s": 4061, "e": 4382, "si": 1}, {"t": "and", "s": 4422, "e": 4522, "si": 1}, {"t": "an", "s": 4522, "e": 4562, "si": 1}, {"t": "apostle", "s": 4562, "e": 5062, "si": 1}, {"t": "of", "s": 5082, "e": 5142, "si": 1}, {"t": "Jesus", "s": 5202, "e": 5563, "si": 1}, {"t": "Christ,", "s": 5623, "e": 6063, "si": 1}, {"t": "according", "s": 6163, "e": 6564, "si": 1}, {"t": "to", "s": 6584, "e": 6664, "si": 1}, {"t": "the", "s": 6704, "e": 6784, "si": 1}, {"t": "faith", "s": 6844, "e": 7104, "si": 1}, {"t": "of", "s": 7144, "e": 7224, "si": 1}, {"t": "God's", "s": 7284, "e": 7564, "si": 1}, {"t": "elect,", "s": 7605, "e": 7985, "si": 1}, {"t": "and", "s": 8685, "e": 8766, "si": 1}, {"t": "the", "s": 8786, "e": 8866, "si": 1}, {"t": "acknowledging", "s": 8906, "e": 9566, "si": 1}, {"t": "of", "s": 9606, "e": 9666, "si": 1}, {"t": "the", "s": 9706, "e": 9786, "si": 1}, {"t": "truth", "s": 9846, "e": 10167, "si": 1}, {"t": "which", "s": 10227, "e": 10387, "si": 1}, {"t": "is", "s": 10427, "e": 10507, "si": 1}, {"t": "after", "s": 10607, "e": 10827, 